if this works the same as SIP,
which is what seems to be

02:51.000 --> 02:56.000
a standard that's out there
amongst voice over IP providers.

02:56.000 --> 03:00.000
Not really, not, but what are
they doing?

03:00.000 --> 03:07.000
What is the peer-to-peer part of
Skype that is so important that
gives it an advantage

03:07.000 --> 03:10.000
over using the SIP protocol?

03:10.000 --> 03:15.000
I can't see any from a user's
perspective and it may not make
any difference the way

03:15.000 --> 03:17.000
telephony is working right now
in voice over IP.

03:17.000 --> 03:22.000
It could of course change with
some of the services, but if you
have any idea please

03:22.000 --> 03:25.000
let me know at adamantcurry.com.

03:25.000 --> 03:30.000
And I'm still looking for a
voice over IP provider and a lot
of people sent me different

03:30.000 --> 03:31.000
links, most of the stuff I'd
already...

03:31.500 --> 03:36.500
