the Netherlands called Rits
Taylor-Kolm who almost offer
what

03:36.500 --> 03:40.500
I'm looking for but I'll just go
through one more time and maybe
you can help me out.

03:40.500 --> 03:42.500
I'm looking for a provider.

03:42.500 --> 03:48.500
It doesn't matter where the
provider is located, as long as
I can get a local dial-up line,

03:48.500 --> 03:54.500
so my own dedicated number in
the Netherlands, that could be
anywhere, preferably Amsterdam,

03:54.500 --> 03:58.500
in Belgium, which is, that's
only optional since we'll only
be here for a couple more

03:58.500 --> 04:01.500
months and definitely one or two
in the States.

04:01.500 --> 04:03.500
I'd love to have a California
number and a New York number.

04:03.500 --> 04:09.500
That way I can call just about
anybody I want and they can also
call me at the very low

04:09.500 --> 04:16.500
cost of voice over IP because
all the pricing seems to be more
or less the same.

04:16.500 --> 04:21.500
Interestingly enough, each
country has its own specific
rates for the mobile telephony
in

04:21.500 --> 04:22.500
