05:42.500 --> 05:48.500
Now, on to iPodder. First of
all, my apologies to Dave
Slusher.

05:50.500 --> 05:55.500
I had commented and I'd given
some feedback on the
Get-Enclosures Perl script
iPodder.

05:56.500 --> 06:00.500
You can find all of these
different versions of iPodder.
They're all designed to do the
same

06:00.500 --> 06:04.500
thing to bring in content into
your iPodder or other mobile mp3
player.

06:06.500 --> 06:10.500
So I've been using his script
instead of my own Apple script
and I'd said that I'm getting
all

06:10.500 --> 06:17.500
kinds of duplicates and all
kinds of crap flying around and
the problem was that I had
incorrectly

06:17.500 --> 06:24.500
entered my cron job. So I had
the hour right and I told you to
run it only these hours,

06:25.500 --> 06:31.500
run it on any day and so I
thought I'd done all the entries
right except at the very
beginning

06:31.500 --> 06:35.500
you have to also specify a
minute otherwise it's going to
run every single minute.

06:36.000 --> 06:41.000
for that entire hour that you
specified and that's why I was
getting all these duplicates and
everything was freaking out.

06:41.000 --> 06:49.000
So it was totally my fault and I
apologize for any implications
that the script was buggy
because it's not. Now it's
working perfectly.

06:49.000 --> 07:00.000
But here's another great
example. I mean the fact that I
even know what a cron job is
puts me way ahead of any user
that you can think of in the
stuff, the people we're making
this stuff for.

07:00.000 --> 07:09.000
And we need to hide that and I
don't mean hide it as much as we
don't want to tell anyone what
we're doing but we need to mask
and just set it up in a much
easier fashion.

07:09.000 --> 07:18.000
So on that very first run it
should say, oh okay I'm going to
install this and it's going to
run every night at 1am and every
morning at 6am.

07:18.000 --> 07:24.000
Is this okay? And you can say
yes for the defaults or you
could specify maybe a couple
different hours.

07:24.000 --> 07:27.000
Maybe just with checkboxes.
Doesn't have to be anything
super big.

07:27.000 --> 07:37.000
Another script that has been
released, another iPodder script
which is now also on the
download directory on
ipodder.org is PyPodder.

07:37.500 --> 07:42.500
